From: Tiago Damascena <tiagobdamascena@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 7 Sep 2026 10:00:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: rk817_charger: a positive battery current is a charge

The status property reports NOT_CHARGING whenever the PMIC's own charge
state machine says CHRG_OFF and the battery current is not negative. On
boards that charge the cell through a separate charger IC and never
route the cable to the RK817's USB input, the state machine stays off
for the whole charge: no plug-in interrupt fires, the USB voltage ADC
reads zero, "online" stays 0 -- while the fuel gauge sees the current
turn positive and the capacity climb.

Measured on an R36S (RK3326, rk817), 6.12.91: cable out, status
"Discharging"; cable in, status "Not charging", charger online 0,
voltage_avg 0, capacity rising. Userspace (EmulationStation's battery
glyph) takes "Not charging" at its word.

Report CHARGING when the charger is off but the average current into
the battery is positive: the sign of the current is the one thing the
PMIC does know, and the driver already trusts it for DISCHARGING.

--- a/drivers/power/supply/rk817_charger.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/rk817_charger.c
@@ -473,7 +473,18 @@
 		}
 		switch (charger->charge_status) {
 		case CHRG_OFF:
-			val->intval = POWER_SUPPLY_STATUS_NOT_CHARGING;
+			/*
+			 * The PMIC's own charger is off, yet current flows
+			 * into the battery: something else is charging it.
+			 * Boards like the R36S feed the cell from a separate
+			 * charger IC and never route the cable to the RK817's
+			 * USB input (no plug-in interrupt, USB voltage reads
+			 * zero), so the current sign is all the PMIC knows.
+			 */
+			if (charger->cur_avg_ua > 0)
+				val->intval = POWER_SUPPLY_STATUS_CHARGING;
+			else
+				val->intval = POWER_SUPPLY_STATUS_NOT_CHARGING;
 			break;
 		/*
 		 * Dead charge is documented, but not explained. I never
